  "question": {
    "text": "The line segment joining <math><mi>A</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mi>B</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>10</mn><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>10</mn><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math> is divided internally in the ratio <math><mn>2</mn><mi></mi><mo>:</mo><mi></mi><mn>3</mn></math> at <math><mi>P</mi></math>. If <math><mi>θ</mi></math> varies, then the perimeter of locus of <math><mi>P</mi></math> is",
